{
  "id": "7e08b5c0-2d28-42cd-b581-912960d708cb",
  "type": "PARENT",
  "data": {
    "body": "Your friend, mass M, jumps up from a crouched position to a vertical standing position, such that their center of mass moves vertically upward through height h. During this process, the point of contact between your friend's feet and the ground is stationary. Your friend experiences a normal force $F_N$ acting upward at the point of contact between the feet and the ground. Your friend's change in translational kinetic energy of center of mass is $\\triangle K_{trans}$, the change in internal energy in the process is $\\triangle E_{int}$, and the change in kinetic energy due to the torso moving relative to the center of mass is $\\triangle K_{rel}$.\n\nAcceleration due to gravity g is downward. Ignore air resistance.",
